A birth's fields offer the existing people and places. When you edit a birth, the Subjects it points at are listed beside its form and open in the same dialog, where you can create a missing person or place too.

== Mapping to CIDOC CRM ==

This dataset partially maps to [http://www.cidoc-crm.org/ CIDOC CRM], via [[Mapping:CIDOC-CRM]]; [[RDF and ontology mappings]] has the export links. The canonical statements run from the event to the person (E67 Birth, P98 brought into life, E21 Person); the reverse "was born" (P98i) is not stored as a separate edge but derived by [[Module:NeoWikiDemo]] reverse-querying the graph, which is how CIDOC inverse properties work.

A person who carries the flat Birth date and Birth place fields instead of a Birth Subject still gets a birth event in the projection: the Mapping synthesizes the E67 Birth and the E52 Time-Span the CIDOC path runs through.

